1:# Storage And Search Backends
3:## Summary
5:Lattice keeps SQLite as the durable source of truth for the graph and memories, but semantic retrieval no longer does brute-force cosine scans on every hot-path query. The daemon now uses a `VectorIndex` abstraction with scoped retrieval and a richer semantic indexing pipeline:
7:- `VectorStore` as the compatibility backend: SQLite BLOB storage plus exact cosine search
8:- `UsearchVectorIndex` as the preferred backend: persisted USearch ANN graph under `.lattice/vectors.usearch`
9:- `VectorScope` to distinguish symbol vectors from file-summary vectors while preserving a compatibility default search path
11:Memory keyword search now uses SQLite FTS5 instead of ad hoc `LIKE` scans.
13:## Vector Indexing
15:- `QueryEngine` depends on `VectorIndex`, not on the SQLite store directly.
16:- SQLite remains the durable source of truth for vectors in `.lattice/vectors.db`.
17:- `vector_keys` stores stable numeric ANN keys for `(file, name, byte_offset)` triples.
18:- `vector_index_meta` stores the configured embedding dimension and a generation counter.
19:- `vectors.usearch.meta.json` records the persisted ANN generation so startup can detect drift and rebuild from SQLite when needed.
21:- The first multi-granularity slice adds deterministic per-file summary vectors alongside symbol vectors.
23:## Sync Model
25:- Cold start: the daemon opens the vector backend, warms from disk if generations match, otherwise rebuilds the ANN file from SQLite.
27:- Incremental sync: watcher updates delete vectors for changed files, re-embed the current nodes for those files, then flush the ANN file.
28:- Embedding payloads now include richer symbol-body anchors such as compact summaries, comments/docstrings, error strings, config keys, and routes before they are written to the vector store.
29:- Failure mode: if USearch initialization or warm-up fails, Lattice falls back to the exact SQLite backend without changing MCP schemas.
31:## Retrieval Pipeline
33:- The query engine now searches both symbol vectors and file-summary vectors before final ranking.
37:## Rollout Observability
39:- Vector sync now logs structured batch stats for mode, backend, graph size, payload size, elapsed time, and throughput.
40:- Watcher-triggered syncs log both vector-sync elapsed time and end-to-end watcher overhead.
43:## Memory Search
45:- `memories.db` remains the source of truth for rows and metadata.
49:  - FTS5 is created if absent
50:  - FTS content is rebuilt from the current non-invalidated memory rows
51:- Store, refresh, promote, invalidate, prune, and clear operations keep FTS rows in sync.
53:## Contract Notes
56:- Runtime storage gains `.lattice/vectors.usearch` and `.lattice/vectors.usearch.meta.json`.
57:- Keyword search semantics stay AND-based, ordered by recency, but are now implemented through FTS5 rather than wildcard table scans.
58:- Symbol-only search remains the compatibility default; file-summary vectors are available through the scope-aware retrieval path.

